// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/petal_jobs_viz.t27 -- petal J (JOBS, petal index 9) of the interactive visualization
; epic. Refs epic t27#12173 (issue t27#12302). Built on specs/t27f/viz_contract.t27; it agrees with row J of
; specs/t27f/petal_viz_plan.t27 (reps 772 = list + badge + timeline, truth VERIFIED).
; --
; What it answers: "which lab jobs are queued, running or done, and of what kind?" The reader sees
; six lab jobs as a list (one line per job: its gate, the gate's class and its state now), as a
; timeline (one cell per job and tick) and as a badge (how many jobs are queued, running and done,
; and the truth label). The reader picks the tick (the stepper) and the node scenario (the choice),
; selects a job or a cell and sees it lit in both views.
; --
; Source of truth: specs/lab/job_kind.t27 (module LabJobKind) is the ONLY place the rules live, and
; this petal calls its pub fns and never copies them: the gate enum and its words (ljk_gate_known,
; ljk_gate_word), the class of a gate (ljk_gate_class), whether a node takes a gate (ljk_node_takes),
; whether the coordinator offers a gate to a node (ljk_offer), the next move after a round of
; receipts (ljk_next), the sample nodes (ljk_sample_desktop, ljk_sample_laptop, ljk_sample_phone) and
; the sample commit (LJK_SHA). The agreement verdict that ljk_next reads is hosting/proof.t27
; job_verdict, with wanted_after for the tiebreak replica.
; --
; Where the states come from: job_kind has no queued, running or done table, so this petal derives
; them and never stores them. A job is QUEUED while ljk_offer does not place it on its node (a
; laptop off mains cannot take a medium or heavy gate: NODE_UNFIT) or before its lease tick. Once
; leased, the receipts that arrive tick by tick go through job_verdict and wanted_after, and
; ljk_next says what happens: ADMIT or VOID ends the job (DONE); WAIT or RETRY keeps it RUNNING.
; The receipt arrivals (PJV_VOTES, PJV_TOP, PJV_SECOND) and the lease ticks (PJV_START) are a
; recorded petal-side fixture, because job_kind keeps no receipt log: the RULES applied to them are
; the source spec's, the arrival data is not. The word of that is in the report, not hidden here.
; --
; Layers of this spec:
;   L1 state     no state of its own: one VizState of the contract, every input through viz_apply.
;                step = the tick (0..4), param = the node scenario (0 recorded, 1 laptops on
;                battery, 2 phones on battery), item = the job.
;   L2 entities  job j = viz_ref(NODE, j); the timeline cell (j, t) = viz_ref(CELL, j * 8 + t);
;                the focus order is the jobs 0..5.
;   L3 rules     pjv_gate, pjv_node, pjv_offer, pjv_state_at: the fixture asked of job_kind.
;   L4 truth     VERIFIED while every value is job_kind's rule over its recorded data; a scenario
;                other than the recorded one is a what-if, so the badge drops to DEMO (viz_may_claim).
;   L5 views     list, timeline and badge, each a plain function of the one VizState.
;   L6 host      pjv_host: the badge, the list and the timeline as three root slots.
; --
; Integer only: no floats, `/` and `%`. Pixel geometry is in frame coordinates (the origin is the
; frame's top-left corner), so a hit test and pjv_host agree without an offset.
; --
; Not claimed: no host draws this petal yet. Wiring it into the glass window
; (specs/t27os/glass_window.t27) is a child issue of the epic.

